all assessment>\"\n}\n\nNote: \"environmental_progression\" scores Environmental Consistency (conditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.4,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.5,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.8,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.65,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.46,\n      \"feedback\": \"The acrolein Strecker pathway (P1) closely tracks the originally proposed Miller-Van Trump route, but all steps (except the first) are mass-imbalanced as shown by the atom balance check. The Strecker sequence is plausible, but the overall pathway fails conservation on several reactions. No reported yields for the full sequence exist, and acrolein's conversion to glutamate has never been demonstrated experimentally. Correct stoichiometries (e.g., explicit H2O for hydrolyses) are missing, and some steps likely need additional ammonolysis or hydrolysis agents to be balanced. Correction required on rxn_002, rxn_003, and rxn_004.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add missing byproducts (likely H2O and/or NH3) to balance mass in hydrolysis and Strecker steps.\",\n        \"Provide explicit stoichiometry or cite literature with full balances.\",\n        \"If hypothesizing this path, flag all but the first step as 'proposed/unconfirmed'.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.3,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.45,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.8,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.65,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.43,\n      \"feedback\": \"The cyanosulfidic photochemical C4 nitrile pathway (P2) is conceptually well-aligned with Patel et al. (2015) but nearly all reactions are severely unbalanced (rxn_005, rxn_006, rxn_002, rxn_003, rxn_004). Mechanistically, the C4 intermediates and photoreductions are plausible, but atom counts fail, indicating major stoichiometric omissions. Hydrolysis and reductive steps are under-specified. Surface/UV conditions are plausible, but Cu(I)/Cu(II) and H2S requirements should be explicit if matching Sutherland conditions.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add balancing species (H2, H2O, NH3, S-product) per mechanistic requirements in all photoreduction and hydrolytic steps.\",\n        \"Clarify need for Cu photoredox if following literature.\",\n        \"Explicitly cite and match stoichiometries from Supplementary Info (Patel et al. 2015), or else indicate proposed-only steps.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.35,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.6,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.45,\n      \"feedback\": \"This \u03b1-ketoglutarate metabolic-analogue route follows the best-supported experimental prebiotic chemistry (glyoxylate/pyruvate + Fe2+, then reductive amination of \u03b1-KG). However, both steps are unbalanced (rxn_007 needs CO2 or O2 byproducts, rxn_008 is off by H2O/O); mass/charge are not conserved as written. Mechanistically, these are real, and conditions (70\u00b0C, Fe2+, pH ~7\u20139) are correct per Muchowska 2019 and Kitadai 2019. Target achievement is upheld only if balances are corrected.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Show the missing byproducts on condensation (CO2 loss, explicit H2O formation on amination).\",\n        \"Adopt explicit stoichiometries from primary sources.\",\n        \"If using FeS or H2/Ni, state required conditions in network legend.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.3,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.2,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.22,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.5,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.6,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.37,\n      \"feedback\": \"The Bucherer\u2013Bergs \u03b1-KG/hydantoin path mirrors recent advances but is entirely unbalanced (rxn_009, rxn_010, and dependent rxn_004), with atom/charge errors unfixable by adding typical small molecules. The concept is literature-backed (Pulletikurti 2022), but hydrolysis and condensation require explicit balancing species. Cyanide and DAP reagent plausibility should be noted.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_009\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add known byproducts (e.g., H2O, CO2, NH3) per hydrolysis and hydantoin equilibria.\",\n        \"Show cyanide/DAP requirements up front.\",\n        \"Cite explicit yields from Pulletikurti et al. if possible, and update reaction balances for network consistency.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.15\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.28,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.5,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.6,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.41,\n      \"feedback\": \"Glycine transamination is valid nonen